WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.164 --> 00:00:00.997
(bright music)

00:00:00.997 --> 00:00:03.378
- Wilderness areas are
incredibly important,

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:06.546
because we need to have
at least a few areas

00:00:06.546 --> 00:00:08.617
that we can go and feel like

00:00:08.617 --> 00:00:12.089
we're still connected somehow to nature.

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:15.140
The wonderful thing is, it's
land that we can all share

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.745
and we can all use,

00:00:16.745 --> 00:00:18.995
and not one person owns it.

00:00:19.921 --> 00:00:21.906
And so, you can come out and feel like

00:00:21.906 --> 00:00:24.489
you kind of own it for the day.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.873
(upbeat music)

00:00:40.544 --> 00:00:41.963
Vermilion Cliffs National Monument

00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:44.341
is on the Arizona-Utah border.

00:00:44.341 --> 00:00:48.008
It encompasses 300,000
acres for public use.

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:53.700
You can go for days
exploring the back country

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.746
and finding all kinds of new discoveries.

00:00:57.746 --> 00:01:00.367
My first job with BLM was back in 2000.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.851
I was stationed at a remote site

00:01:02.851 --> 00:01:04.497
out in the middle of all this,

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.936
and I fell in love with it
and didn't want to leave.

00:01:06.936 --> 00:01:10.204
I feel like my job is to
help educate the public

00:01:10.204 --> 00:01:12.537
to protect places like this.

00:01:13.427 --> 00:01:15.669
Vermilion Cliffs is most iconically known

00:01:15.669 --> 00:01:17.046
for the wave.

00:01:17.046 --> 00:01:18.468
It is gorgeous.

00:01:18.468 --> 00:01:21.251
It is an undulating slick rock sandstone,

00:01:21.251 --> 00:01:22.995
but the wave is not the only feature

00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:25.186
in this beautiful country.

00:01:25.186 --> 00:01:27.595
There are so many other things to explore

00:01:27.595 --> 00:01:30.678
if you're willing to make the effort.

00:01:33.046 --> 00:01:33.888
(lively piano music)

00:01:33.888 --> 00:01:37.109
White Pocket requires
incredible commitment

00:01:37.109 --> 00:01:37.942
to get here.

00:01:37.942 --> 00:01:41.301
Skills to navigate some pretty tough roads

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.909
and you're dealing with a lot

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:46.250
of Mother Nature's worst elements.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.928
Getting here is a big reward.

00:01:48.928 --> 00:01:50.428
I'm free out here.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.031
A lot of us kind of scratch our heads

00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:55.639
because we don't understand

00:01:55.639 --> 00:01:57.955
how a landscape like this can be formed,

00:01:57.955 --> 00:02:00.554
but all of these things
are shaped by Mother Nature

00:02:00.554 --> 00:02:02.971
over about 190 million years.

00:02:04.978 --> 00:02:08.609
And so it's pretty
incredible and fascinating

00:02:08.609 --> 00:02:10.784
to marvel at how long it's taken

00:02:10.784 --> 00:02:13.367
to create this great sculpture.

00:02:14.543 --> 00:02:16.998
The beauty of this place,

00:02:16.998 --> 00:02:20.165
you can't compare it to anything else.

00:02:26.704 --> 00:02:29.454
(digital jingle)

